  "reason": "Q1/Q2 PASS => the naive R499 port is NOT refuted on availability or on declared-order grounds (no lane is starved, and the A-anchor x order is strictly increasable on In5 in all three families). It is also SOUND (丙 = 甲's constraints + extra ones => every 丙 solution is a legal design routing). But EQUIVALENCE (same solution set) is NOT yet decided: the decisive question is whether a legal double-layer routing can realize an inversion of two lanes that are BOTH on In5 at one of these cuts (a swap done earlier in a wide zone via In4). The naive monotone constraint forbids exactly that. That test needs the R513-T5 max-flow PATHS, which the registered artifact does not store. => Q3 UNDECIDED, hence per #K2-189 §四: a 丙-UNSAT may NOT be used for any design-level conclusion until Q3 is closed; a 丙-SAT is a valid milestone either way (soundness).",
  "consequence_per_k2189_s4": "⇒ 在 Q3 关闭之前，丙 的 **UNSAT 支不可用**（同乙之病），**SAT 支有效**。⇒ ENG 建议：**先只读关闭 Q3**（复算 R513-T5 最大流路径，多项式、0 求解），再决定把唯一一次受证求解花在『naive 序变量版』（若 Q3 证等价）还是『保真换位记账版』（若 Q3 证不等价，规格见 faithful_replacement_spec）。",
